            <h2>3. Personal Data We Process</h2>

            <p>
                Depending on how you use our website and software, we may
                process the following categories of personal data:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Name and contact details</li>
                <li>Email address</li>
                <li>Telephone number, where provided</li>
                <li>Company and business information</li>
                <li>Account and login information</li>
                <li>Information submitted through contact or demo requests</li>
                <li>Technical information required to operate the service</li>
                <li>Security and usage information</li>
            </ul>


            <h2>4. Contact and Demo Requests</h2>

            <p>
                If you contact us by email, telephone or another available
                communication channel, we process the information you provide
                in order to respond to your request and, where applicable,
                arrange a consultation or demonstration.
            </p>

            <p>
                Depending on the circumstances, the legal basis for processing
                may be Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where processing is necessary to
                take steps at your request prior to entering into a contract,
                or Article 6(1)(f) GDPR where processing is based on our
                legitimate interests.
            </p>


            <h2>5. User Accounts</h2>

            <p>
                If you create an account for Warehouse Management, we process
                the information required to create and maintain your account,
                authenticate you and provide the requested services.
            </p>

            <p>
                This may include account information, login credentials and
                other information required for the proper operation and
                security of the service.
            </p>


            <h2>6. Warehouse Management Data</h2>

            <p>
                Warehouse Management allows users to manage business and
                warehouse-related information.
            </p>

            <p>
                Depending on the features used, this may include information
                relating to:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Products</li>
                <li>Categories</li>
                <li>Warehouses</li>
                <li>Storage locations</li>
                <li>Suppliers</li>
                <li>Customers</li>
                <li>Orders</li>
                <li>Inventory levels</li>
                <li>Stock movements</li>
                <li>Documents and business records</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
                Where customers enter personal data into Warehouse Management,
                the customer remains responsible for ensuring that such
                processing is lawful and that an appropriate legal basis exists.
            </p>


            <h2>7. Server Logs and Technical Data</h2>

            <p>
                When you access our website or software, technical information
                may be processed automatically by the systems used to operate
                the service.
            </p>

            <p>
                Depending on the configuration of the hosting environment,
                this may include IP address, date and time of access, browser
                type, operating system, requested pages, technical error
                information and similar technical data.
            </p>

            <p>
                Such processing may be necessary to ensure the security,
                stability and proper operation of our services.
            </p>


            <h2>8. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>

            <p>
                Our website and software may use technically necessary cookies
                or similar technologies required for functions such as
                authentication, sessions and security.
            </p>

            <p>
                Where analytics, marketing or other non-essential technologies
                are used, they will be implemented in accordance with
                applicable data protection requirements and, where required,
                based on your consent.
            </p>


            <h2>9. Authentication and Security</h2>

            <p>
                We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to
                protect personal data against accidental or unlawful
                destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure or
                unauthorised access.
            </p>

            <p>
                Access to protected areas of the Warehouse Management system
                requires authentication where applicable.
            </p>


            <h2>10. Data Retention</h2>

            <p>
                We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to
                fulfil the purposes for which it was collected or where we are
                legally required to retain it.
            </p>

            <p>
                Once the relevant purpose has ended and no statutory retention
                obligation applies, personal data will be deleted or
                anonymised where technically and legally appropriate.
            </p>


            <h2>11. Service Providers and Recipients</h2>

            <p>
                We may use technical service providers to operate our website,
                software, infrastructure and communication services.
            </p>

            <p>
                Where required by applicable law, appropriate contractual
                safeguards are established with service providers that process
                personal data on our behalf.
            </p>


            <h2>12. International Data Transfers</h2>

            <p>
                If personal data is transferred to recipients located outside
                the European Economic Area, such transfers will only take place
                where the requirements of applicable data protection law are
                fulfilled.
            </p>


            <h2>13. Your Rights</h2>

            <p>
                Depending on the applicable legal requirements, you may have
                the following rights regarding your personal data:
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>Right of access</li>
                <li>Right to rectification</li>
                <li>Right to erasure</li>
                <li>Right to restriction of processing</li>
                <li>Right to data portability</li>
                <li>Right to object to processing</li>
                <li>Right to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
            </ul>


            <h2>14. Right to Lodge a Complaint</h2>

            <p>
                You have the right to lodge a complaint with a competent data
                protection supervisory authority if you believe that the
                processing of your personal data violates applicable data
                protection law.
            </p>


            <h2>15. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>

            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time in order
                to reflect changes to our services, technical processes or
                applicable legal requirements.
            </p>

            <p>
                The version published on this website is the current version
                applicable at the time of your visit.
            </p>


